# TypeScript

Do not use `any`, `Record<string, any>`, or `@ts-ignore`.

Prefer a named domain type for each request and response:

```ts
interface AnalyzeDocumentRequest {
  documentId: string;
  prompt: string;
}

interface AnalyzeDocumentResponse {
  id: string;
  summary: string;
  confidence: number;
  createdAt: string;
}

async function analyzeDocument(
  payload: AnalyzeDocumentRequest,
): Promise<AnalyzeDocumentResponse> {
  return apiClient.post("/analyze", payload);
}
```

Do not suppress TypeScript errors. Fix the type or narrow it.
